<header><p class="st-kicker">other · British Isles</p><h1 class="st-title">Lordship of Mann</h1><p class="st-meta">1333 CE – 1765 CE (approx.) · capital Castletown</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Isle of Man under English lords, above all the Stanley earls of Derby, who ruled it as 'Kings' and then 'Lords of Mann' for over three centuries.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-perth">Treaty of Perth</a> of 1266 Man passed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a>, but it changed hands repeatedly in the Anglo-Scottish wars. From 1333 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edward-iii-of-england">Edward III</a> granted it to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-montagu-1st-earl-of-salisbury">William Montagu</a>, later Earl of Salisbury, and English rule became permanent. In 1405 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-iv-of-england">Henry IV</a> granted the island to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-stanley-died-1414">Sir John Stanley</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Stanleys styled themselves <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lord-of-mann">Kings of Mann</a> until 1504 and then Lords of Mann. The island kept the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tynwald">Tynwald</a>, its own laws and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manx-language">Manx language</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/james-stanley-7th-earl-of-derby">James Stanley, 7th Earl of Derby</a>, held it for Charles I, and his wife, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charlotte-stanley-countess-of-derby">Charlotte de la Tremoille</a>, defended it until 1651. Smuggling flourished in the 18th century because of low duties.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The lordship passed to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/duke-of-atholl">Dukes of Atholl</a> in 1736. To end smuggling, the British government bought the sovereign rights with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/revestment-act-1765">Revestment Act</a> of 1765, creating the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crown-dependencies">Crown Dependency</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/isle-of-man">Isle of Man</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/lordship-of-mann.jpg" alt="Lordship of Mann" width="320" height="336"><figcaption>Image: Sémhur · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kingdom_of_Mann_and_the_Isles-en.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1333 CE – 1765 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Castletown</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>William Montagu, John Stanley, James Stanley, 7th Earl of Derby</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Manx, English</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Isle of Man</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Isle of Man (lordship), Kingdom of Mann</dd></dl></aside></div>
